# XTON Smart Contract Audit Report

## Overview

This folder contains a public smart contract audit report for **XTON**, a TON ecosystem wallet and Web3 access layer.

Softstack audited **XTON Core** smart contract infrastructure, providing security review support for a project positioned around wallet functionality, dApp access, and user interaction within the TON ecosystem.

## About XTON

**XTON** is a TON-focused wallet and Web3 gateway designed for the TON blockchain. Public project descriptions position XTON as a functional wallet for creating accounts, managing assets, interacting with dApps, and accessing TON-based Web3 services.

That makes XTON relevant as more than a simple token. It is part of the user access and interaction layer for the TON ecosystem.

## Why This Project Matters

XTON is significant because wallet and gateway products sit close to the end user and often act as an access layer into broader blockchain activity.

That makes this audit a strong public reference for:

- TON ecosystem security
- wallet-related blockchain infrastructure
- Web3 access layer smart contract audits
- core smart contract security
- security work tied to user-facing blockchain infrastructure

For buyers and partners, this is useful because security around wallet-adjacent and access-layer products directly affects trust, usability, and user safety.

## TON Ecosystem Relevance

XTON publicly positions itself as a wallet and gateway to Web3 apps on TON. Listings in TON ecosystem directories also describe XTON as a non-custodial TON wallet with support for dApp interaction, multi-account functionality, smart contract interaction, and related user-facing features.

This gives the project relevance as part of the broader TON user experience stack.

